Subject: GameCube controls for GameCube controllers
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Charged's engine is Super Mario Strikers': DetInput keeps its GameCube kind
(DET_CONTROLLER_GAMECUBE), which remaps every game action through the
GameCube table (gGameCubeButtonRemap). Retail Charged never creates a
GameCubePad, so its players are all Wii Remotes with Nunchuks.

A GameCube controller whose gamepad profile plays with GameCube controls
(the launcher's choice, a host setting outside the tweak mask) becomes that
kind again. DetInput::ReadFromPad takes the controller's own buttons, analog
L/R and C-stick from the host (mscharged_tweak_gamecube_pad) instead of the
Nunchuk's, with no motion and no pointer; the left stick stays the Nunchuk
stick, which the host moves with the controller's stick. Pass, shoot and
charge, the lob modifier, switching players and using an item then come out
on Super Mario Strikers' buttons by themselves.

Charged turned four of SMS's button actions into Wii gestures, read in four
functions. For a GameCube DetInput they read SMS's buttons again, decided as
SMS does from who has the ball:

- cAIPad::DetectRightShake (big hit): Y, without the ball.
- cAIPad::DetectLeftShake (cycle the item): Z.
- cFielder::GetDekePadDirection and IsDekePadPressed (deke, slide tackle and
  the special move, on the D-pad in Charged): with the ball the C-stick dekes
  toward itself and Y toward the stick; without it, B slide-tackles while the
  other team has the ball. R does the special move. The D-pad keeps working
  as in Charged.

The conversion happens where the local input is captured, so the packed
record (buttons, 4-bit triggers, sticks) and its connection kind carry it to
the match, replays and other peers, whose hooks read the same kind. A
GameCube player gives the goalie's Mega Strike defence no pointer: as with
any player that is not a Wii controller, a teammate on one defends it or
nobody does (GoalieActions.cpp). The pause menu resets the input as before.

These are the controls of the Strikers WiiCompiled port's GameCube support
(its runtime's msc_game.cpp), here on the decompiled sources.

diff --git a/src/Game/AI/Fielder.cpp b/src/Game/AI/Fielder.cpp
index 66b3552..9d6b463 100644
--- a/src/Game/AI/Fielder.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/AI/Fielder.cpp
@@ -3324,8 +3324,63 @@ bool cFielder::IsReceivePassDekeRequested(unsigned short* direction)
     return false;
 }
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// Port: GameCube controls (DetInput.cpp). Charged moved Super Mario Strikers'
+// deke and slide tackle onto the D-pad; a GameCube player has them on SMS's
+// buttons again, decided as SMS does from who has the ball: with it, the
+// C-stick dekes toward itself and Y (action 29) toward the stick; without it,
+// B (action 25) slide-tackles while the other team has the ball. R does what
+// the D-pad does in Charged (the special move). The angle is in screen space
+// like the D-pad's: the left stick's way, or with the stick centred the way
+// the player faces. Afterwards the D-pad works as in Charged.
+static bool GameCubeDekeDirection(cFielder* fielder, unsigned short* direction)
+{
+    DetInput* input = fielder->GetGlobalPad();
+    if (input == 0 || input->GetControllerType() != DET_CONTROLLER_GAMECUBE)
+        return false;
+    // The game's fast square root gives NaN for a centred stick.
+    const float left = input->m_PolarAnalogLeft.r;
+    const unsigned short move = left == left && left > 0.3f
+        ? input->m_PolarAnalogLeft.a
+        : (unsigned short)(fielder->GetActualFacing() - input->m_aRemapAngle);
+    if (fielder->HasBall())
+    {
+        const float cStick = input->m_PolarAnalogRight.r;
+        if (cStick == cStick && cStick > 0.3f)
+        {
+            *direction = input->m_PolarAnalogRight.a;
+            return true;
+        }
+        if (input->IsPressed(29, true))
+        {
+            *direction = move;
+            return true;
+        }
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        cPlayer* owner = g_pBall != 0 ? g_pBall->GetOwner() : 0;
+        if (owner != 0 && owner->GetTeam() != fielder->GetTeam() && input->IsPressed(25, true))
+        {
+            *direction = move;
+            return true;
+        }
+    }
+    if (input->m_ButtonBitfield & 0x0020) // PAD_TRIGGER_R
+    {
+        *direction = move;
+        return true;
+    }
+    return false;
+}
+#endif
+
